00:03:00.970 --> 00:03:01.803
A heart attack.

00:03:01.803 --> 00:03:04.060
So, when a patient has a heart attack,

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:06.710
as they described at a ST elevation MI,

00:03:06.710 --> 00:03:07.960
it's called a STEMI,

00:03:07.960 --> 00:03:10.300
you got to get a patient right away

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:11.780
into the cath lab, which is where

00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:13.850
they put a catheter from your artery,

00:03:13.850 --> 00:03:15.980
either from down below or from your arm,

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:18.440
into your heart and either open it up

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:20.390
with a stent or just evaluate

00:03:20.390 --> 00:03:22.100
and see if you even need
a stent to begin with.

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:23.780
- And there's a very strict protocol

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:24.970
as to how much time it is

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:26.419
