00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:50.250
Let's explain what a
dobutamine stress echo is.

00:07:50.250 --> 00:07:51.790
So, an echocardiogram

00:07:51.790 --> 00:07:53.160
is an ultrasound of the heart.

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:54.730
You can give a chemical which actually

00:07:54.730 --> 00:07:57.050
stresses the heart, makes
it beat more rapidly,

00:07:57.050 --> 00:07:59.440
which, therefore makes
more blood flow occur.

00:07:59.440 --> 00:08:00.690
Now, you can look at the echo

00:08:00.690 --> 00:08:01.980
and see how the heart responds,

00:08:01.980 --> 00:08:03.370
to see if the walls of the heart

00:08:03.370 --> 00:08:04.640
are moving appropriately,

00:08:04.640 --> 00:08:05.990
if blood flow is circulating

00:08:05.990 --> 00:08:07.660
appropriately within the heart.

00:08:07.660 --> 00:08:10.750
But now, why are they
doing a test like that

00:08:10.750 --> 00:08:12.902
