- They're gonna crack his
chest in the elevator.

00:09:08.916 --> 00:09:09.960
- No they're not, no they're not, no.

00:09:09.960 --> 00:09:10.890
- [Alex] Dude, we're not moving.

00:09:10.890 --> 00:09:13.800
- Really, you think?

00:09:13.800 --> 00:09:15.330
- You need a strong hand

00:09:15.330 --> 00:09:17.530
and a pair of sharp
trauma shears right now.

00:09:19.534 --> 00:09:20.840
- Oh.

00:09:20.840 --> 00:09:22.210
- That doesn't really happen.

00:09:22.210 --> 00:09:23.870
- We have generators.

00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:25.180
- [Preston] How's the patient?

00:09:25.180 --> 00:09:26.530
- He's not looking so good.

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:32.620
- You're a doctor and
that's your explanation

00:09:32.620 --> 00:09:33.453
of what's happening?

00:09:33.453 --> 00:09:34.879
Give the rhythm, give the pulse.

00:09:34.879 --> 00:09:37.110
- Have you even even
heard of the Hmong people?

00:09:37.110 --> 00:09:39.530
Our religion has got
rules that are way old

00:09:39.530 --> 00:09:41.380
and way set in stone, and way spiritual

00:09:41.380 --> 00:09:43.752
and you don't mess with them.

00:09:43.752 --> 00:09:46.203
And you don't anger the ancestors.

00:09:47.360 --> 00:09:49.860
Even if you pierce your
tongue and play in a band.

00:09:51.360 --> 00:09:53.273
- What are the rules, exactly?

00:09:53.273 --> 00:09:55.340
- Good, when encountering a situation

00:09:55.340 --> 00:09:57.400
with a patient that culturally,

00:09:57.400 --> 00:10:00.030
it's something that you
are not familiar with,

00:10:00.030 --> 00:10:02.160
smartest question thus far in the show,

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:03.150
what are the rules?

00:10:03.150 --> 00:10:04.760
By knowing that, you might be able

00:10:04.760 --> 00:10:06.130
to find a point of compromise

00:10:06.130 --> 00:10:07.450
to fix the situation.

00:10:07.450 --> 00:10:08.450
- Apparently Anna's father believes

00:10:08.450 --> 00:10:09.550
she's missing something

00:10:09.550 --> 00:10:10.700
that she needs for surgery.

00:10:10.700 --> 00:10:11.533
- Missing something?

00:10:11.533 --> 00:10:13.563
Missing what?
- One of her souls.

00:10:14.690 --> 00:10:15.880
We don't need a social worker,

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:17.093
we need a shaman.

00:10:18.083 --> 00:10:18.940
- Get a shaman.

00:10:18.940 --> 00:10:21.143
- You definitely did
not have a heart attack.

00:10:22.317 --> 00:10:24.401
- So I can go home?

00:10:24.401 --> 00:10:28.200
- Not yet, your EKG
shows significant changes

00:10:28.200 --> 00:10:29.080
and I'm gonna find out why

00:10:29.080 --> 00:10:30.390
before you leave the hospital.

00:10:30.390 --> 00:10:31.870
- Got to get home.

00:10:31.870 --> 00:10:33.570
- Pete, you're in a hospital.

00:10:33.570 --> 00:10:34.903
- [Pete] Need to get home.

00:10:36.340 --> 00:10:38.240
- So when you lose a lot of blood

00:10:38.240 --> 00:10:39.500
you become hypoxic.

00:10:39.500 --> 00:10:41.260
You're brain's not
getting enough blood flow.

00:10:41.260 --> 00:10:42.340
When your brain doesn't
get enough blood flow

00:10:42.340 --> 00:10:43.560
it doesn't get enough oxygen.

00:10:43.560 --> 00:10:44.900
When your brain doesn't get enough oxygen,

00:10:44.900 --> 00:10:47.500
it starts saying crazy things like,

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:49.250
you're in the middle of
an elevator that's stuck,

00:10:49.250 --> 00:10:50.440
bleeding out from your chest

00:10:50.440 --> 00:10:51.273
from a gun shot wound

00:10:51.273 --> 00:10:52.550
and you say you want to go home.

00:10:52.550 --> 00:10:53.580
- O'Malley, blood pressure.

00:10:53.580 --> 00:10:55.027
- I've taken it three times.
- And?

00:10:55.027 --> 00:10:57.832
- I can't hear a systolic over 50.

00:10:57.832 --> 00:10:59.130
(whistling)

00:10:59.130 --> 00:11:00.160
- So that's quite dangerous,

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:01.490
that means he's not getting profusion

00:11:01.490 --> 00:11:02.610
to his vital organs,

00:11:02.610 --> 00:11:04.480
including his liver, brain, and kidneys,

00:11:04.480 --> 00:11:05.560
which means that those organs

00:11:05.560 --> 00:11:06.680
are currently dying.

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:07.550
- I'll be right back.

00:11:07.550 --> 00:11:09.030
- Wait, where are you going?

00:11:09.030 --> 00:11:10.500
- To get an instrument tray.

00:11:10.500 --> 00:11:12.806
You guys are going to
have to open up his chest.

00:11:12.806 --> 00:11:14.100
- Hot damn.

00:11:14.100 --> 00:11:15.610
- I'm just gonna have to get a shaman,

00:11:15.610 --> 00:11:18.160
today, in the hospital.

00:11:18.160 --> 00:11:20.200
- Shaman's aren't listed
in the yellow pages.

00:11:20.200 --> 00:11:22.540
Our shaman is 500 miles from here.

00:11:22.540 --> 00:11:23.830
You are an arrogant man.

00:11:23.830 --> 00:11:27.050
- No, I'm just a guy with
access to a helicopter.

00:11:27.050 --> 00:11:28.970
- Cool, let's see how
this is gonna happen.

00:11:28.970 --> 00:11:30.560
- Hey, where are you two going so fast?

00:11:30.560 --> 00:11:31.890
- Burke is talking George and Alex

00:11:31.890 --> 00:11:33.890
through heart surgery in the elevator.

00:11:33.890 --> 00:11:37.080
- Shepherd's setting up
a shaman healing ritual.

00:11:37.080 --> 00:11:37.980
- [Izzie] Rock on!

00:11:39.175 --> 00:11:40.313
- I have porn guy.

00:11:41.510 --> 00:11:43.940
- This show is really medically inaccurate

00:11:43.940 --> 00:11:45.780
but it's hilarious.
- It is, it's funny.

00:11:45.780 --> 00:11:47.350
- She has the porn guy.
- That's funny.

00:11:47.350 --> 00:11:49.320
- Wouldn't have residency
been much more fun

00:11:49.320 --> 00:11:50.153
if it was like this?

00:11:50.153 --> 00:11:52.140
We didn't have to
operate in the elevators,

00:11:52.140 --> 00:11:54.000
we didn't have shaman,

00:11:54.000 --> 00:11:55.880
we just had patients who had no insurance

00:11:55.880 --> 00:11:58.110
that we had to battle
to get them treatment.

00:11:58.110 --> 00:12:00.100
- You never shaved your legs.
- What?

00:12:00.100 --> 00:12:00.933
- [Preston] But be sure you don't

00:12:00.933 --> 00:12:02.020
cut in to the lung or heart.

00:12:02.020 --> 00:12:04.250
- How can I be sure of that?

00:12:04.250 --> 00:12:06.106
- You just have to be sure.

00:12:06.106 --> 00:12:08.000
(laughing)

00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:10.050
- On this date, for the past seven years,

00:12:10.050 --> 00:12:12.821
you have what looks like a heart attack.

00:12:12.821 --> 00:12:16.620
- No, no, I know I've had
some scares but I don't--

00:12:16.620 --> 00:12:18.523
- Every year on this date?

00:12:19.460 --> 00:12:21.100
- Is there some significance to this date

00:12:21.100 --> 00:12:22.110
for you personally?

00:12:22.110 --> 00:12:23.340
- No.

00:12:23.340 --> 00:12:24.173
Nothing.

00:12:24.173 --> 00:12:25.520
- What were you doing the first year,

00:12:25.520 --> 00:12:27.420
the first time you had a cardiac episode?

00:12:27.420 --> 00:12:30.260
- Oh, I couldn't remember back that far.

00:12:30.260 --> 00:12:31.540
- We were in the yard.

00:12:31.540 --> 00:12:33.210
I remember because our neighbor,

00:12:33.210 --> 00:12:34.110
what was his name?

00:12:35.180 --> 00:12:36.013
- Ted.

00:12:36.013 --> 00:12:39.580
- That's right, he died
of an aneurism I think,

00:12:39.580 --> 00:12:41.690
and we watched as the funeral home people

00:12:41.690 --> 00:12:44.857
took him away and you
had your first attack.

00:12:44.857 --> 00:12:46.310
- And you were close to Ted?

00:12:46.310 --> 00:12:48.152
- No, we barely knew Ted.

00:12:48.152 --> 00:12:49.672
- She shaved her legs.

00:12:49.672 --> 00:12:51.343
If this is takotsubo's
I'm gonna smack you,

00:12:51.343 --> 00:12:52.571
I'm telling you right now.

00:12:52.571 --> 00:12:53.404
- Come on, that's impressive.

00:12:53.404 --> 00:12:54.640
- [George] It's beating a little stronger.

00:12:54.640 --> 00:12:56.910
- [Preston] Excellent,
keep your finger there.

00:12:56.910 --> 00:12:58.203
- Okay, now what?

00:12:59.790 --> 00:13:02.123
- That's it.
- That's it?

00:13:06.570 --> 00:13:07.660
- What's wrong with that picture?

00:13:07.660 --> 00:13:09.950
- There's open flame in a hospital.

00:13:09.950 --> 00:13:11.770
- And why is open flame in a hospital,

00:13:11.770 --> 00:13:13.770
especially in that bed, really dangerous?

00:13:13.770 --> 00:13:15.520
- You've got oxygen around there.

00:13:15.520 --> 00:13:17.330
- Oxygen's a little flammable.

00:13:17.330 --> 00:13:19.313
- Oh, it potentiates the fire, yeah.

00:13:20.480 --> 00:13:21.313
- Poof.

00:13:21.313 --> 00:13:23.481
- You have stress cardiomyopathy.

00:13:23.481 --> 00:13:24.314
- Cardiomyopathy.

00:13:24.314 --> 00:13:26.110
- Bravo Dr. Mike.

00:13:26.110 --> 00:13:28.180
- I have an offer from Boston General.

00:13:28.180 --> 00:13:30.210
- You took it to get away.

00:13:30.210 --> 00:13:31.540
We swore we'd never talk again

00:13:31.540 --> 00:13:33.080
about what we had together.

00:13:33.080 --> 00:13:34.540
- This reminds me of The Notebook.

00:13:34.540 --> 00:13:36.180
You guys ever watch The Notebook?

00:13:36.180 --> 00:13:37.827
Romantic movie.
- I didn't see it.

00:13:37.827 --> 00:13:38.760
- You didn't see it?
- No.

00:13:38.760 --> 00:13:41.293
- We should watch it, like a bro night.

00:13:42.500 --> 00:13:44.140
- Yeah, no.
(laughing)

00:13:44.140 --> 00:13:45.995
- It takes away his pain.

00:13:45.995 --> 00:13:48.233
You see, the thing is, Henry?

00:13:49.180 --> 00:13:50.530
Henry takes away my pain.

00:13:50.530 --> 00:13:51.773
- Humans are weird.

00:13:53.010 --> 00:13:54.533
All of us, myself included.

00:13:55.440 --> 00:13:58.630
- Well, we're all unique
and again, whatever.

00:13:58.630 --> 00:14:01.260
- Did you just use a synonym for weird?

00:14:01.260 --> 00:14:03.020
In a more positive tone?

00:14:03.020 --> 00:14:05.150
- Yeah.
- Usually you're the dark one.

00:14:05.150 --> 00:14:05.983
- I am, I am.

00:14:05.983 --> 00:14:08.217
I don't know, I'm in a
good mood today, but yeah.

00:14:08.217 --> 00:14:09.146
- It's probably 'cause of the porn.

00:14:09.146 --> 00:14:09.980
- It must be the porn.

00:14:09.980 --> 00:14:10.953
- Choose me.

00:14:12.130 --> 00:14:13.003
Love me.

00:14:18.470 --> 00:14:20.740
I'll be at Joe's tonight so if you do

00:14:20.740 --> 00:14:25.003
decide to sign the papers, meet me there.

00:14:27.140 --> 00:14:29.990
- Oh, no, you didn't like it?

00:14:29.990 --> 00:14:31.683
Too narcissistic for your taste?

00:14:32.830 --> 00:14:33.683
Pick me.

00:14:34.540 --> 00:14:36.450
I hope you enjoyed our little collab here.

00:14:36.450 --> 00:14:38.470
If you want to see a
playlist of all my collabs

00:14:38.470 --> 00:14:41.865
with Ricky, Ava, Gabby, Molly, click here.

00:14:41.865 --> 00:14:42.764
Do it, say click here.

00:14:42.764 --> 00:14:43.597
- Click here.

00:14:43.597 --> 00:14:45.865
- And stay happy and healthy.

